A fire alarm detector is a safety device that senses smoke, heat or flame signatures and triggers an audible/visual alert to warn occupants of an emerging fire. The unit may operate as a standalone sensor or be networked within an integrated fire‑alarm system, linking multiple detectors to a central control panel for coordinated response. Upon detection it can activate alarms, dial emergency services, engage sprinkler systems or notify building management through IoT‑enabled communication channels.
