What is a Fire Alarm Detector?
Fire alarm detectors are essential components of fire‑protection systems, designed to provide early warning of combustion events. Modern detectors incorporate advanced sensing principles-such as photoelectric smoke detection, infrared flame sensing, and heat‑based thermal detection-to achieve rapid and reliable fire identification. When integrated with building‑automation platforms, these devices can also deliver real‑time status updates, support predictive maintenance, and enable coordinated emergency responses across HVAC, access control and security subsystems.
